.TH FUZZYGENE 1 2000-1月 "fuzzygene_modules" "fuzzygene_modules"
.SH NAME
fuzzygene_modules \- The coarse grained module layer (FCM): module assignment, bounded steady state and warm start.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIfuzzygene_modules(\fBfuzzygene\fR as <generic> FuzzyGeneModel, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The coarse grained module layer (FCM): module assignment, bounded steady state and warm start.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBfuzzygene\fB \fR\- a trained model built with \fBfcmWarmStart = TRUE\fR. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment used to report errors. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a named list of data.frames
.PP
.SH DETAILS
.PP
Returns a named list:
 


 
- \fBtable\fR: \fBgene\fR / \fBmodule\fR / \fBbaseline\fR, the module assignment
 computed at fit time (only present when \fBfcmWarmStart = TRUE\fR);
- \fBmodules\fR: \fBmodule\fR / \fBn_genes\fR / \fBactivation\fR, the bounded
 activation of the module level fuzzy cognitive map on the training baseline;
- \fBinitial\fR: \fBgene\fR / \fBwarm_start\fR / \fBsurrogate\fR, the per gene
 initial state derived from the module state (this is what the root finder starts from).
- \fBsummary\fR: \fBavailable\fR / \fBmodule_count\fR / \fBconverged\fR /
 \fBsteps\fR / \fBperiod\fR / \fBnotes\fR.


 


 The module layer is bounded by construction, so it always terminates with either a fixed
 point or a detected limit cycle. It is a **rough** skeleton: the module average erases the
 individual genes, which is why the default is off and the surrogate must never replace the
 per gene prediction.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
FuzzyGene
.SH FILES
.PP
